A request to an exclusive arena looks in the chunks of every bin.

The arenas give each chunk the bin of the first thing that is placed in it, and
a page of one slice is never placed in a chunk of another bin, to reduce
fragmentation. A request that finds nothing in one arena goes on to the next,
or has a new arena reserved.

A heap with an exclusive arena (mi_heap_new_in_arena()) has nowhere else to go.
In an arena of two chunks, once a page of eight slices was the first in the
second chunk, requests for small blocks failed when the first chunk was full,
with most of the arena free.

Where the search in an exclusive arena has found nothing, it goes through the
chunks of all bins. A search that finds room runs the same instructions as
before, and so does every search in another arena.

--- a/src/arena.c
+++ b/src/arena.c
@@ -2133,6 +2133,7 @@
   // init bitmaps
   uint8_t* base = mi_arena_start(arena) + bitmap_base;
   arena->slices_free = mi_arena_bbitmap_init(subproc, slice_count, &base);
+  arena->slices_free->is_of_exclusive_arena = exclusive;
   arena->slices_committed = mi_arena_bitmap_init(slice_count, &base);
   arena->slices_dirty = mi_arena_bitmap_init(slice_count, &base);
   arena->slices_purge = mi_arena_bitmap_init(slice_count, &base);
